WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.391 --> 00:00:04.630
- [Narrator] On March 2nd,
SpaceX CEO, Elon Musk,

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.590
announced his plan to create
a new city called Starbase

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.120
in what is now Boca Chica Village,

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.430
a tiny, unincorporated community

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.100
of about 30 homes,

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.870
located next to the
southernmost beach in Texas.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.270
Musk's tweet, and his updates
encouraging his followers

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.850
to move to the Brownsville,
South Padre area

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.690
has created a surge of
interest in local real estate,

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.990
mostly from outside buyers.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.850
- We probably will not
see anything like this

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.110
in our lifetime.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:33.943
Who knows if Brownsville

00:00:33.943 --> 00:00:35.480
will ever have an
opportunity like this again.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.230
We certainly haven't in the past.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.930
- [Narrator] But while
many in the state welcome

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.520
the increased investment, and jobs,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.980
some in south Texas worry
that SpaceX's expansion

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.500
will come at a steep price

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.673
to the local people and the environment.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.263
- They, in effect,

00:00:51.263 --> 00:00:53.340
have shut down me
personally and economically.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.513
- They nickeled and dimed us to death.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.310
- [Narrator] SpaceX did not respond

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.530
to multiple requests for comment.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.120
The question now is how will Elon Musk

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.830
build his gateway to Mars

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.003
in the face of a local backlash?

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.110
The conflict centers around control

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.640
of a state highway that is the only road

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.980
to both SpaceX's rocket testing site

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.620
and a beloved community beach.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.110
Texas Highway 4,

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.820
which is known locally
as Boca Chica Boulevard,

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.790
is a two-lane road that stretches

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.850
from the shores of Boca Chica Beach

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.263
to the city of Brownsville.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.110
- After he did his tweet,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.310
it really changed things a lot.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.580
- [Narrator] Craig Grove has
been a real estate broker

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.620
in the Brownsville area for 11 years.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.770
- We get calls, like I said,

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.410
from all over the United States

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.840
and even outside of the United States.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.030
My phone volume, I have
a answering service,

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.943
it's probably doubled or quadrupled.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.220
I know of properties
that were on the market

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.740
for a good long time that didn't sell

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.760
and now because of Elon's tweet,

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.690
they ended up going for cash offers.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:06.210
If even a fraction of what
SpaceX wants to do happens,

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.310
it's gonna change the face of Brownsville.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.540
A lot of the people that
live in these houses

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.210
are SpaceX engineers.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.254
And then if you look behind me over here,

00:02:15.254 --> 00:02:17.540
this is a brand new subdivision

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.490
that's gonna be opening up.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.623
So you can see it's happening.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.850
- [Narrator] SpaceX has had
a footprint in Boca Chica

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.920
since 2012 but the aerospace company

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:33.000
didn't begin ramping up
work at the site until 2019

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.900
when it began scaling up development

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.965
of its Starship spacecraft.

00:02:36.965 --> 00:02:38.780
(rocket whooshing)

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.720
- Starship is the largest
flying object ever made.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.500
- [Narrator] This is the same
vehicle NASA recently selected

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.493
to return humans to the moon in 2024.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.890
- Best memories of my life
are right here on this beach.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.053
Now I have to check if it's okay to go.

00:02:57.053 --> 00:02:59.570
(waves crashing)

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:02.210
- Bobby Lerma still lives
down the street from the beach

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:05.713
on land that has been in his
family for five generations.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:10.033
- I would like to describe
Boca Chica Beach as a paradise.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.890
This is what I want to protect.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:16.480
I want my kids and grandkids

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.383
to come here like I did.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.610
- [Narrator] Until recently, Boca Chica,

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.530
which sits at the edge of
a national wildlife refuge

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.590
was a favorite spot for locals looking

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.280
for a quiet escape.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.640
Endangered sea turtles and
ocelots call the refuge home,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.440
as well as scores of migratory birds.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.400
But since SpaceX began expanding
its operations in 2019,

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.597
conservationists worry

00:03:40.597 --> 00:03:42.960
that the eventual environmental impact

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.963
will be devastating.

00:03:45.171 --> 00:03:48.620
(rock crashing)

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.635
(playful music)

00:03:50.635 --> 00:03:51.630
In just a few years,

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.030
the area surrounding Boca
Chica has been transformed.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.470
- I have to go through,

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.100
ask permission to come to my own home.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.850
SpaceX had security people

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:03.100
of their own bossing everybody around

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.091
and requiring IDs

00:04:05.091 --> 00:04:08.360
and things that aren't
necessary for a public highway.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.090
- [Narrator] An FAA spokesperson said

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.860
that in December of 2020,

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.500
the agency approved a request by SpaceX

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.810
to increase the closure
hours to 300 hours annually.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.820
He said implementation and enforcement

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.160
of those agreements was a local matter.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.290
In Texas, public access
to Gulf Coast beaches

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.390
is a right enshrined in
the state's constitution.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:32.690
But in 2013, Cameron County
received a special exemption

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.270
from state lawmakers

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.540
to temporarily close the
beach and the highway

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.943
during rocket launches.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.890
Today, some locals say this
privilege has been abused.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.910
And that the frequent highway closures

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.670
have essentially privatized the beach.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:51.020
In a phone conversation with The Journal,

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.077
Cameron County Judge Eddie Trevino said,

00:04:54.077 --> 00:04:56.260
"We want SpaceX to succeed,

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.860
but not at the expense of the community.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.260
If they think they'll be
able to take over the highway

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.997
or the beach, they're mistaken."

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.500
Texas House Representative,
Alex Dominguez,

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.830
said he has found a bill

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.890
to limit beach access
closures at Boca Chica

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.150
but he's working with SpaceX officials

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.130
to try to improve beach access

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:18.747
without limiting SpaceX's
allowed closures.

00:05:18.747 --> 00:05:20.530
(dramatic music)

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:22.580
SpaceX has faced the most friction

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.800
from the residents of Boca Chica Village.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.450
- Not only did they move in
and change the whole tone

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:29.990
and tenor of the place

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:33.590
but they began to do 24/7 construction,

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:36.670
which meant wall-to-wall people,

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:41.070
cars, traffic, noise,
lighting, you name it.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.750
- [Narrator] Cheryl Stevens
was a homeowner for 15 years

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.360
in the village and grew
up going to the beach.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.940
Like many former Boca
Chica Village residents,

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.310
Stevens purchased the property thinking

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.780
it would be her retirement home.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.090
- There was no way to stay.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.350
I mean, it was just so stressful.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:57.680
- [Narrator] Over the past year,

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.010
multiple SpaceX rockets have exploded,

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.480
breaking windows, scattering
debris and causing fires.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.090
- I mean, it was really basically the gun

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.090
to the head approach.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.640
Not a lot of negotiation on the price

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.390
and a lot of thinly veiled threats

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.230
of eminent domain.

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:15.706
- [Narrator] Stevens
said she sold to SpaceX

00:06:15.706 --> 00:06:20.706
in late 2019 for more than $139,500.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.350
But she characterized the
company's initial offers

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.273
as unfair and predatory.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.870
For his part, Bobby Lerma said
he will continue speaking out

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.240
about the road closures.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.810
- They are kind of pesky
at calling me every day

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.470
about whether I wanna sell

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.970
but I'm not going anywhere

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.690
and I'm not be bullied by anybody.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:41.750
I'm gonna fight back.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.600
Why? Because it is my backyard.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.630
So I have to protect my backyard

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:46.837
'cause nobody else will.

00:06:46.837 --> 00:06:51.837
(dramatic music)
(waves crashing)

